WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.043 --> 00:00:04.796
What I love about this trip is that
it's an opportunity

00:00:04.796 --> 00:00:07.966
to explore places that I haven't
had a chance to explore before. 

00:00:19.477 --> 00:00:21.646
We are setting out from Toronto,

00:00:21.646 --> 00:00:24.858
but we're taking the slow
road up through Muskoka, 

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:27.402
cross through Algonquin Park,
through the Ottawa Valley,

00:00:27.402 --> 00:00:29.195
and eventually down to Montreal. 

00:00:36.911 --> 00:00:39.247
The Muskoka Region lends itself
to cranberry growing  

00:00:39.247 --> 00:00:40.623
because of the acidic soil.

00:00:40.623 --> 00:00:41.666
It's a miracle fruit. 

00:00:46.254 --> 00:00:47.922
I know what you're thinking.

00:00:48.506 --> 00:00:50.508
How do I get me one of these? 

00:01:06.816 --> 00:01:07.734
I grew up in Toronto. 

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:10.695
I've seen leaves
and I've appreciated the color, 

00:01:10.695 --> 00:01:12.781
but this is something
altogether different. 

00:01:12.781 --> 00:01:14.574
This is a sea of color,

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:16.659
and you can't capture it in any other way

00:01:16.659 --> 00:01:18.912
except to stand there and see it for yourself.

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:24.417
You have to make a stop at
Henrietta's Pine Bakery.

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:25.919
It's like the thing to do.

00:01:26.211 --> 00:01:30.799
57 years I think they've been
serving up these Muskoka clouds. 

00:01:32.217 --> 00:01:33.593
Really, really good.

00:01:34.969 --> 00:01:37.806
One of the reasons that people
come to Algonquin Park 

00:01:37.806 --> 00:01:39.182
for the fall colors is the fact that it's so accessible. 

00:01:39.182 --> 00:01:40.683
There's just nothing like it anywhere else. 

00:02:18.721 --> 00:02:21.641
Kanatha-Aki means the land without frontier.

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:26.271
My horse, your horse.

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:33.361
In general, our company needs to
reconnect people with the nature, animals. 

00:02:34.195 --> 00:02:35.530
This is that new bus.

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:36.447
Ok.

00:02:37.615 --> 00:02:40.577
You know what makes
this part of the world unique

00:02:40.577 --> 00:02:44.038
is that you quickly feel
a part of something.

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:48.501
It was brighter and bolder
than I thought it would be. 

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:51.254
There were far more adventures
to be had than I expected. 

00:02:51.254 --> 00:02:55.425
Incredible culture, fantastic food,
beautiful landscapes. 

00:02:55.592 --> 00:02:56.634
It's all right here. 

